<title>USA: U.S. cocoa and coffee exports--Commerce.</title>
<headline>U.S. cocoa and coffee exports--Commerce.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department cocoa and coffee exports, in tonnes:</p>
<p> -				 Domestic   Foreign</p>
<p> -				  Exports   Re-Exports</p>
<p> -  Cocoa Beans-X:   Jan 97     Nil     565</p>
<p> -			 Dec 96     Nil     545</p>
<p> -			 Jan 96     Nil     416</p>
<p> - Cocoa Butter-Y:   Jan 97     316     529</p>
<p> -			 Dec 96     245     382</p>
<p> -			 Jan 96     115     410</p>
<p>X-Whole or broken, raw or roasted. Y-Fat and oil included.  </p>
<p>    COFFEES --    Jan97     Dec96     Jan96</p>
<p>DOMESTIC EXPORTS (tonnes) --</p>
<p>    -  Unroasted     61	 137	  92</p>
<p>    -    Roasted  1,665     1,839     1,228</p>
<p>    Concentrated    227	 282	 354</p>
<p>FOREIGN RE-EXPORTS (tonnes) --</p>
<p>    -  Unroasted  4,142     4,234     3,741</p>
<p>    -    Roasted  1,112     1,009	  93</p>
<p>    Concentrated     19	 Nil	   6</p>
<p>Coffees include decaffeinated and nondecaffeinated, and exclude husks and skins. Concentrated includes instant and nonflavored.</p>
</text>
